#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""pokectl: the Hermes agents' narrow window into POKE.

Standard library only, so it runs on the droplet with no installs. Config comes
from /etc/pokectl.env (override with POKECTL_ENV): POKE_BASE_URL, AGENT_API_TOKEN,
and optionally TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID.

Agents never get a shell. They get tools from `pokectl mcp --role support|pm`, which reuse
the command functions below (the Support bot: policy, ticket get|recent|classify|reply;
the PM bot: ticket get, backlog list|get|create|attach|update, request_assessment, request_followup, recommend, budget;
the Design-Engineer: backlog get, read-only repo tree|read|search, submit_assessment, answer_followup).
A systemd timer calls: sync (which hands tickets to the PM, sends finished-ticket and
recommendation cards, acts on Zach's decisions, and alerts on stuck tasks, all to
Telegram with zero model tokens) and usage-sync.
The maintainer calls: report, ticket story, backlog list|get, budget.
"""

